8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:04\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"I don’t think this is the expected result; in any case—whether it’s middleware or something else—it should be able to retrieve the file again.\\n\\nI think we may need to investigate this issue further.\\n\\n**flc1125** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-11T13:59:33Z\\n\\nBased on this PR, I’ve provided a prototype reference: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8161\\n\\n@dmathieu @akats7, take a look and see how it works if we adjust it according to the prototype.\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-11T15:42:57Z\\n\\n@flc1125 can you clarify which behavior you’re referring to as incorrect, are you referring to \\n\\n```\\n\\nrequire.ErrorIs(t, err, fs.ErrNotExist)\\n\\n```\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-12T01:28:14Z\\n\\nI thought we had already agreed on the `RemoveAll` approach? Naturally, if you call RemoveAll, the temporary files are deleted and can’t be accessed afterward. Since this happens during the middleware’s return phase, I’d expect that most middlewares wouldn’t read the multipart form at that point anyway. I’m not sure if the implications of RemoveAll were discussed in the SIG meeting, but it might be worth confirming.\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-12T10:24:52Z\\n\\n@flc1125 I’m still not clear on the result you’re referring to, the result aligns to my understanding of what we’ve discussed.\\n\\nAlso I’m not sure if your prototype fix would work, I think it still doesn’t address the core issue which is that when we originally set c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(ctx) with an unparsed form the http server won’t know to clean it up. I don’t think Cloning the request solves that.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-01]\\n\\n# Pull Request: fix(otelgin): remove multipartform temporary file (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#6609)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"i don t think this is the expect result in ani case whether it s middlewar or someth els it should be abl to retriev the file again i think we may need to investig this issu further flc1125 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 11t13 59 33z base on this pr i ve provid a prototyp refer http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8161 dmathieu akats7 take a look and see how it work if we adjust it accord to the prototyp akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 11t15 42 57z flc1125 can you clarifi which behavior you re refer to a incorrect are you refer to requir errori t err f errnotexist yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 12t01 28 14z i thought we had alreadi agre on the removeal approach natur if you call removeal the temporari file are delet and can t be access afterward sinc this happen dure the middlewar s return phase i d expect that most middlewar wouldn t read the multipart form at that point anyway i m not sure if the implic of removeal were discuss in the sig meet but it might be worth confirm akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 12t10 24 52z flc1125 i m still not clear on the result you re refer to the result align to my understand of what we ve discuss also i m not sure if your prototyp fix would work i think it still doesn t address the core issu which is that when we origin set c request c request withcontext ctx with an unpars form the http server won t know to clean it up i don t think clone the request solv that sourc id src pr 01 pull request fix otelgin remov multipartform temporari file open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 6609\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"074e174c8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"d2c20958070b5cb8\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.37883389853854094, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1655651836264871, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8764609, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"074e174c8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:04\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"I would lean towards the solution proposed by the SIG: only support configurability when users explicitly request it. After all, enabling configurability after `RemoveAll()` is an operation that ensures both extensibility compatibility and backward compatibility.\\n\\n@akats7 @dmathieu \\n\\n---\\n\\n**akats7** — 2025-11-10T02:01:52Z\\n\\nAh gotcha, didn't see that that was mentioned. I'm good on holding off until it's explicitly requested.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**akats7** — 2025-11-10T04:27:26Z\\n\\n@Yiling-J I think we're good to resolve the conflicts and close this out, thanks!\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Yiling-J** — 2025-11-10T11:58:48Z\\n\\nI’ve resolved the conflicts, and the otelgin package tests passed on my machine @flc1125 @dmathieu @akats7 \\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-11-10T14:02:53Z\\n\\nCould you add the corresponding unit tests for this scenario?\\n\\n> My only concern with RemoveAll is on the off chance that a middleware further up the chain still expect access to the form data.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Yiling-J** — 2025-11-10T15:21:14Z\\n\\n> Could you add the corresponding unit tests for this scenario?\\n\\n> \\n\\n> > My only concern with RemoveAll is on the off chance that a middleware further up the chain still expect access to the form data.\\n\\nI’ve added more details to the test case, it now includes two extra middlewares, one upstream and one downstream, to demonstrate what happens when `RemoveAll` is called in the otel middleware. The behavior is correct to me, but let’s confirm that we all agree it’s the expected one.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-01]\\n\\n# Pull Request: fix(otelgin): remove multipartform temporary file (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#6609)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609  \\n\\n**Author**: Yiling-J  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-01-13T13:45:43Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-13T01:26:12Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: open  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/gin_multipartform` → `main`  \\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"i would lean toward the solut propos by the sig onli support configur when user explicit request it after all enabl configur after removeal is an oper that ensur both extens compat and backward compat akats7 dmathieu akats7 2025 11 10t02 01 52z ah gotcha didn t see that that wa mention i m good on hold off until it s explicit request akats7 2025 11 10t04 27 26z yile j i think we re good to resolv the conflict and close this out thank yile j 2025 11 10t11 58 48z i ve resolv the conflict and the otelgin packag test pass on my machin flc1125 dmathieu akats7 flc1125 2025 11 10t14 02 53z could you add the correspond unit test for this scenario my onli concern with removeal is on the off chanc that a middlewar further up the chain still expect access to the form data yile j 2025 11 10t15 21 14z could you add the correspond unit test for this scenario my onli concern with removeal is on the off chanc that a middlewar further up the chain still expect access to the form data i ve ad more detail to the test case it now includ two extra middlewar one upstream and one downstream to demonstr what happen when removeal is call in the otel middlewar the behavior is correct to me but let s confirm that we all agre it s the expect one sourc id src pr 01 pull request fix otelgin remov multipartform temporari file open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 6609 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609 author yile j creat 2025 01 13t13 45 43z updat 2025 11 13t01 26 12z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state open branch fix gin _ multipartform main\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"074e174c8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"4e46763026cba535\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3763417085385409, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.16556518362648706, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8681536, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"074e174c8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:04\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"I haven’t tested yet, but I think it should work. However, I’m considering opening an issue in Go to get their suggestions. Since it’s closely related to the `http` package and the `WithContext` method is widely used by middlewares and frameworks, I think they might be able to suggest best practice for this situation.\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-27T12:14:50Z\\n\\n@akats7 It seems I can’t get any help from the Go team. I’m not in favor of parsing the form in the middleware, as this step should be explicitly done by the user. Parsing large forms can consume resources, and the `ParseMultipartForm` function has a `maxMemory` parameter that should also be decided by the user.\\n\\nAfter giving this more thought over the past few days, I believe this is more of a Go design issue. The `WithContext` and `ParseMultipartForm` behavior is implicit, hard to notice, poorly documented, and lacks a clear best practice solution. I think the reattach approach might be better because it’s less aggressive and can likely be safely applied to other OpenTelemetry middlewares facing the same issue. The only downside, compared to `RemoveAll`, is that it relies on other middlewares to also handle `WithContext` and `ParseMultipartForm` correctly. If all middlewares do the right thing, `net/http` should eventually clean up the temporary files automatically.\\n\\n**flc1125** on `CHANGELOG.md` — 2025-11-10T14:01:14Z\\n\\n```suggestion\\n\\n- Fix issue in `go.opentelemetry.io/contrib/instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin` middleware where temporary files for multipart/form-data were not being removed. (#6609)\\n\\n```\\n\\n**flc1125** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-11-10T14:03:40Z\\n\\nClose to reduce distractions.\\n\\n**flc1125** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 117) — 2025-11-10T14:03:54Z\\n\\nClose to reduce distractions.\\n\\n**flc1125** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-11T13:20:30Z\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"i haven t test yet but i think it should work howev i m consid open an issu in go to get their suggest sinc it s close relat to the http packag and the withcontext method is wide use by middlewar and framework i think they might be abl to suggest best practic for this situat yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 27t12 14 50z akats7 it seem i can t get ani help from the go team i m not in favor of pars the form in the middlewar a this step should be explicit done by the user pars larg form can consum resourc and the parsemultipartform function ha a maxmemori paramet that should also be decid by the user after give this more thought over the past few day i believ this is more of a go design issu the withcontext and parsemultipartform behavior is implicit hard to notic poor document and lack a clear best practic solut i think the reattach approach might be better becaus it s less aggress and can like be safe appli to other opentelemetri middlewar face the same issu the onli downsid compar to removeal is that it reli on other middlewar to also handl withcontext and parsemultipartform correct if all middlewar do the right thing net http should eventu clean up the temporari file automat flc1125 on changelog md 2025 11 10t14 01 14z suggest fix issu in go opentelemetri io contrib instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin middlewar where temporari file for multipart form data were not be remov 6609 flc1125 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 11 10t14 03 40z close to reduc distract flc1125 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 117 2025 11 10t14 03 54z close to reduc distract flc1125 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 11t13 20 30z\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"074e174c8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"73fa157d3c7a0345\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3675360932047535, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.16058327600679068, \"vector_similarity\": 0.850426, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"074e174c8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:04\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"the HTTP server holds the original request, and using otelgin.Middleware replaces the request with [c.request = c.request.WithContext(ctx)](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/blob/cb45b36c145ff13e4ba76fd9e02ef39297c906b5/instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gintrace.go#L79), causing subsequent c.FormFile reads to fall on the new request. As a result, the original request held by the HTTP server does not have the MultipartForm, preventing it from being destroyed.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-01]\\n\\n# Issue: Using otelgin.Middleware will cause temporary MultipartForm files not to be destroyed. (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#5946)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946  \\n\\n**Author**: zacklpx  \\n\\n**Created**: 2024-07-25T03:50:39Z · **Updated**: 2025-07-03T13:28:05Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: open  \\n\\n**Labels**: bug, area: instrumentation, instrumentation: otelgin  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Discussion (11)\\n\\n**Yiling-J** — 2025-01-11T11:28:03Z\\n\\n@akats7 Is there any plan to address this issue? For reference, a similar problem was resolved in Echo with this fix: [Echo-contrib PR #90](https://github.com/labstack/echo-contrib/pull/90/files#diff-86bf6c8ade26d5c58be942ac6765d89c8855c8713ba9a4d61249e16e3fa9c0fc).  If you're busy, I'd be happy to help by creating a PR to address it. Let me know!  \\n\\n---\\n\\n**dmathieu** — 2025-01-12T13:54:25Z\\n\\ncc @akats7 as code owner.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**akats7** — 2025-01-13T02:11:01Z\\n\\nHi @Yiling-J,\\n\\nFeel free to open a PR, I'll gladly review\\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-07-02T08:35:01Z\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"the http server hold the origin request and use otelgin middlewar replac the request with c request c request withcontext ctx http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib blob cb45b36c145ff13e4ba76fd9e02ef39297c906b5 instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gintrac go l79 caus subsequ c formfil read to fall on the new request a a result the origin request held by the http server doe not have the multipartform prevent it from be destroy sourc id src issu 01 issu use otelgin middlewar will caus temporari multipartform file not to be destroy open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 5946 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 5946 author zacklpx creat 2024 07 25t03 50 39z updat 2025 07 03t13 28 05z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state open label bug area instrument instrument otelgin mileston discuss 11 yile j 2025 01 11t11 28 03z akats7 is there ani plan to address this issu for refer a similar problem wa resolv in echo with this fix echo contrib pr 90 http github com labstack echo contrib pull 90 file diff 86bf6c8ade26d5c58be942ac6765d89c8855c8713ba9a4d61249e16e3fa9c0fc if you re busi i d be happi to help by creat a pr to address it let me know dmathieu 2025 01 12t13 54 25z cc akats7 a code owner akats7 2025 01 13t02 11 01z hi yile j feel free to open a pr i ll glad review flc1125 2025 07 02t08 35 01z\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"074abb7e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"id\": \"0190cf7fa5b9729f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.36652470320475344, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.16058327600679065, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8470547, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"074abb7e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 16121, \"chunk_count\": 10, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:04\", \"token_count\": 5002, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609  \\n\\n**Author**: Yiling-J  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-01-13T13:45:43Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-13T01:26:12Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: open  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/gin_multipartform` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +95 / -0 across 3 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Timeline\\n\\n- 2025-01-13T13:45:44Z · **review_requested** by Yiling-J\\n\\n- 2025-01-13T13:45:57Z · **review_requested** by github-actions[bot]\\n\\n- 2025-01-